title: Mo_Start_Day2
---
<<declare $mo_playing_cards to false>>
<<declare $mo_friends to false>>
<<declare $mo_waddles_enemies to false>>

<<if $mo_playing_cards is false and $mo_friends is false and $mo_waddles_enemies is false>>
    Mort: I can't say that I find it pleasant to be seeing you again so soon.
    Mort: Please don't take offense.
        -> You: *smile stupidly* Non taken!
            Mort: *in a mocking, high pitched voice* Non taken!
        -> You: Mrs. Mort, I must insist that you comply and answer my questions truthfully.
            Mort: It depends.
            You: ...
            You: It depends on what?
            Mort: On whether or not the others were truthful.
            Mort: I would find it rather annoying to be the only one who is putting their neck on the line.
                -> You: Why would you be putting your neck on the line if you didn't do anything wrong.
                    Mort: Seems like we won't know for sure until the grand reveal in the end.
                    Mort: Exciting stuff.
                -> You: Huh, I never really took into consideration that they could be lying.
                    Mort: Glad I could be of service in that way.
                -> You: I have a nose for the truth, Mrs. Mort.
                    Mort: I can tell.
                    Mort: *looks at your nose disapprovingly*
    You: *You shake you head and compose yourself*
    You: We've got a mystery to solve.
    Mort: It's funny how Waddles manages to hunt us from the grave, isn't it?
<<elseif $mo_playing_cards is true or $mo_friends is true or $mo_waddles_enemies is true>>
    Mort: This would be a great place to leave it off.
<<endif>>
 -> You: \[playing cards\] Do these playing cards belong to you? <<if $mo_playing_cards is false and $playing_cards is true>>
    <<jump Mo_PlayingCards>>
 -> You: Is there anyone in the circus that you feel close to? <<if $mo_friends is false>>
    <<jump Mo_Friends>>
 -> You: Did the deceased have any enemies that you were aware of? <<if $mo_waddles_enemies is false>>
    <<jump Mo_WaddlesEnemies>>
 -> You: I agree, Let's pick up where we left off again tomorrow.
    Mort: If you insist. *rolls her eyes*
===

title: Mo_PlayingCards
---
<<set $mo_playing_cards to true>>

<<declare $mo_borrowed to false>>
<<declare $mo_stolen to false>>

<<if $mo_borrowed is false and $mo_stolen is false>>
    Mort: *tries to snatch them from you*
    You: *pull the cards away last second*
    Mort: Where did you find these? I have been looking for them everywhere.
    You: As you might be able to gather from the context in which the current conversation is taking place, I have found this set of cards whiles searching the crime scene.
    Mort: But that is impossible, I don't recall being at the crime scene.
    You: That's what I would say as well if I was the murderer.
    Mort: Very funny, detective. Who says that you did not indeed were the one to snuff old Waddles out like a candle?
    You: *prolonged eye contact*
    Mort: *prolonged eye contact*
<<elseif $mo_borrowed is true xor $mo_stolen is true>>
    Mort: *starts to tap her fingers in wait*
<<else>>
    <<jump Mo_Start_Day2>>
<<endif>>
    -> You: Did you borrow the cards to anyone else? <<if $mo_borrowed is false>>
        <<jump Mo_Borrowed>>
    -> You: Is it possible that the cards were stolen from you? <<if $mo_stolen is false>>
        <<jump Mo_Stolen>>
===

title: Mo_Friends
---
<<set $mo_friends to true>>

Mort: Are we talking about closeness in proximity or emotionally.
You: Ehm, ehm... Both!
Mort: Hm, Poppet enjoys to be close to me, way to close for my comfort. I think she does that with everyone though.
Mort: It is a little bit creepy if you ask me. 
Mort: Gives me the heebie jeebies.
Mort: But if we were to talk about friendships, I do find Teddy very fun to be around.
    -> You: That's nice. What do you like about Teddy?
        Mort: He looks really funny. Have you met him and his hat? 
        Mort: Sometimes he even falls over, because the hat is too heavy for him.
        Mort: Bahahahah *doubles over and holds her stomach, laughing*
        Mort: *wipes a tear from her eye as she calms down*
        Mort: Ah, I like Teddy.
<<jump Mo_Start_Day2>>
===

title: Mo_WaddlesEnemies
---
<<set $mo_waddles_enemies to true>>

Mort: Would you feign surprise if I told you that he did?
Mort: Of course he had enemies. He was terribly annoying and constantly parading about as if he ran this place.
Mort: He should be grateful to have lived such a long life, considering how much of a nuisance he was.
You: My files tell me that he was a mere 35 years of age.
Mort: Exactly.
<<jump Mo_Start_Day2>>
===

title: Mo_Borrowed
---
<<set $mo_borrowed to true>>

Mort: I never lend my belongings to anyone, given that all of them are infused with magic of some sort.
Mort: Alright, maybe "never" and "anyone" are quite strong words. 
Mort: I'm a selfish detective. I do share.
Mort: For instance, I handed Teddy some of my handkerchiefs to help with his sniffles.
Mort: The cards are just not the kind of item I would hand of to the untrained, as they are not to me meddled with.
    -> You: Why are your cards not to be meddled with?
        Mort: *smirks in a sinister way*
        Mort: 
        Mort:
        You: *shudder*
<<jump Mo_PlayingCards>>
===

title: Mo_Stolen
---
<<set $mo_stolen to true>>
Mort: That does sound like something that Waddles would have done.
Mort: But why don't I believe it? Something is telling me that that is not what happened.
Mort: *paces up and down*
Mort: *stops* abruptly*
Mort: The cards were in Waddles wagon because he confiscated them from me. There, mystery solved.
    -> You: Did you just make that up?
        Mort: No, it happened a couple of days ago, when I was in the middle of winning my round of poker.
        Mort: That silly penguin with his silly hat interrupted me with his loud and incessant knocking.
        Mort: I believe he would have knocked down the whole door, but since it was just Waddles we are talking about here, all I heard were those weird flopping sounds that his flippers made on the brass door.
        Mort: *shudders*
        Mort: He yet again complained about the noise and took the cards with him into his den.
        Mort: Darn it, I really wished I could have strangled the smug grin off of his face, ut it appears I am late to the party.
        Mort: Talking of late, *yawns* are we done here soon?
<<jump Mo_PlayingCards>>
===
